{
  "id": "COMPOUND:16888 - PROTEIN:1107",
  "verbalization": "Theasaponin E1 is implicated in the regulation of Serine/threonine-protein kinase B-raf through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Theasaponin E1 acts as a target of K-252a, which in turn targets B-raf. This indicates a potential regulatory relationship where Theasaponin E1 may influence B-raf through K-252a, possibly by modulating the activity of the phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate 3-kinase C2 domain-containing subunit beta or the solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1. These targets are all involved in signaling and transport processes that could modulate B-raf activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Theasaponin E1 may influence B-raf, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
